WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.622
Lab 1 runs in the kit's folder
against two fictional exports:

3
00:00:04.622 --> 00:00:08.625
an HR-to-Entra inbound job, and
a SailPoint source that creates

4
00:00:08.625 --> 00:00:12.550
accounts and updates department,
title and office location.

5
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.988
Step one runs the
chapter's tests: six pass.

6
00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:18.288
Step two checks the two exports.

7
00:00:18.288 --> 00:00:22.971
Entra inbound writes eight attributes
and SailPoint writes seven,

8
00:00:22.971 --> 00:00:25.563
with one Finding, one Warn and two Info.

9
00:00:25.563 --> 00:00:28.180
The Finding is department: both update it,

10
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.799
so each overwrites the other
and the drift never settles.

11
00:00:31.799 --> 00:00:33.300
The command exits one.

12
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.875
Step three maps SailPoint's title to
Entra ID's job title, and runs it again.

13
00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:42.237
Now there are two Findings:
job title joins department.

14
00:00:42.237 --> 00:00:46.270
Without the alias, the second
writer of job title was invisible.
